/target

# NOTE: running the tool from the repo root drops a generated project here (e.g.
# `cargo run -- --name blinky` creates ./blinky). Those carry their own
# Cargo.toml + .cargo/config.toml pinning a bare-metal target, which
# rust-analyzer auto-discovers and then fails to analyse:
#   "can't find crate for `test`"  (no_std targets have no test crate)
# Generate outside the repo instead:
#   cargo run -- --chip xiao-rp2040 --name demo --out /tmp/demo
